<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.9.6: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01012</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.9.6: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>9be46ff2-f497-4ef2-ba4c-fd0b9c70d320</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section>
      <para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
      <!--Do not edit this div tag.  It must surround the interaction block-->
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <exercise id="fb4582f9-6add-436e-a74f-586af09e3a74" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>The graphs show the distance, \(d\), traveled by two cars, A and B, over time, \(t\). Distance is measured in miles, and time is measured in hours. Which car traveled slower? 
          <figure><media alt="Lines A and B on coordinate plane."><image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_12_11_01.svg"/></media></figure></para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>Car A</para>
            <para>Car B</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Car A traveled slower because Car B was a farther distance in the same amount of time as Car A.</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.9.1 – 4.9.4.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is Car A traveled slower because Car B was a farther distance in the same amount of time as Car A.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_43d7eb08-a3ef-4608-a848-3f943fd46fcc" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>For questions 2 – 5, use the graphs below to match each description of a situation in which the volume of water in a tank is a function of time to its corresponding graph.</para>
            <div class="os-raise-d-flex os-raise-justify-content-between">
              <div class="os-raise-mx-auto">
                <para>Graph 1
            <figure><media alt="Graph on coordinate plane, no grid, Origin O. V shaped graph, line begins on Y axis, Vertex points down."><image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_12_11_02.svg"/></media></figure></para>
              </div>
              <div class="os-raise-mx-auto">
                <para>Graph 2
            <figure><media alt="Graph on coordinate plane, no grid, Origin O. Line begins at origin, moves upwards and to right. Steeper second segment."><image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_12_11_03.svg"/></media></figure></para>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="os-raise-d-flex os-raise-justify-content-between">
              <div class="os-raise-mx-auto">
                <para>Graph 3
            <figure><media alt="Graph on coordinate plane, no grid, Origin O. V shaped graph, line begins on at origin, Vertex points up."><image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_12_11_04.svg"/></media></figure></para>
              </div>
              <div class="os-raise-mx-auto">
                <para>Graph 4
            <figure><media alt="Graph on coordinate plane, no grid, Origin O. Line begins at origin, moves upwards and to right, decreases briefly, then increases again."><image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_12_11_05.svg"/></media></figure></para>
              </div>
            </div>
            <para>An empty 20-gallon water tank is filled at a constant rate for 3 minutes until it is half full. Then, it is emptied at a constant rate for 3 minutes.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Graph 3</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.9.1 – 4.9.4.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is Graph 3.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_04a914d5-1a20-4a61-8d16-2929c8a4328f" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>A full 10-gallon water tank is drained for 30 seconds, until it is half full. Afterward, it gets refilled.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Graph 1</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.9.1 – 4.9.4.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is Graph 1.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_1fb4f2f9-3fd6-4178-9685-d6fece3b0815" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>A 2,000-gallon water tank starts out empty. It is being filled for 5 hours, slowly at first, and faster later.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Graph 2</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.9.1 – 4.9.4.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is Graph 2.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_594de829-a3ec-448e-8b1c-b95c36a43989" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>An empty 100-gallon water tank is filled in 50 minutes. Then, a dog jumps in and splashes around for 10 minutes, letting 7 gallons of water out. The tank is refilled afterward.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Graph 4</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.9.1 – 4.9.4.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is Graph 4.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <para>For questions 6 – 7, use this situation and function:</para>
      <para>
        <quote>The daily cost to the manufacturing company is modeled by the function \(C(x)=7.25x+2500\), where \(C(x)\) is the total daily cost and \(x\) is the number of items manufactured.</quote>
     </para>
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <exercise id="f14d1917-2b7c-42b3-9389-2b0ff44689fc" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para> What value equals \(C(0)\)?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! 2500</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.9.1 – 4.9.5.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is 2,500.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="fa3eeebd-3640-4077-bc4e-fd233737d66e" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>What does \(C(0)\) mean in the context of the situation?</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>When the cost is 0</para>
            <para>Horizontal intercept</para>
            <para>Cost before any items are manufactured</para>
            <para>Maximum cost</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Cost before any items are manufactured</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.9.1 – 4.9.5.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is cost before any items are manufactured.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <!--Do not edit below this line-->
      <solution> </solution>
      <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response"> </div>
    </section>
  </content>
